<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/main.css" />
    <title><%= title%></title>
    <style>
        .credits-container {
            max-width: 900px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 40px 20px;
        }
        .credits-container h1 {
            font-size: 48px;
            margin-bottom: 4px;
            color: #f5f2ea;
        }
        .credits-container .subtitle {
            color: #6b6558;
            font-size: 16px;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
        }

        .credit-card {
            background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03);
            border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);
            border-radius: 12px;
            padding: 24px 28px;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }
        .credit-card h2 {
            color: #f5f2ea;
            margin: 0 0 12px 0;
            font-size: 20px;
            border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);
            padding-bottom: 10px;
        }
        .credit-card .name {
            font-size: 18px;
            font-weight: 600;
            color: #f5f2ea;
        }
        .credit-card .role {
            color: #6b6558;
            font-size: 14px;
            margin-left: 12px;
        }
        .credit-card p {
            color: #b5aea0;
            margin: 6px 0;
            font-size: 14px;
            line-height: 1.6;
        }
        .credit-card .year {
            color: #4a9d6e;
            font-weight: 600;
        }

        .system-section {
            background: rgba(255,255,255,0.02);
            border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.04);
            border-radius: 12px;
            padding: 24px 28px;
            margin-top: 10px;
        }
        .system-section h3 {
            color: #f5f2ea;
            font-size: 18px;
            margin: 0 0 12px 0;
        }
        .system-section p {
            color: #b5aea0;
            font-size: 14px;
            line-height: 1.8;
            margin: 8px 0;
        }
        .system-section ul {
            color: #b5aea0;
            font-size: 14px;
            line-height: 2;
            padding-left: 20px;
            margin: 8px 0;
        }
        .system-section li {
            margin-bottom: 4px;
        }
        .system-section strong {
            color: #e9e6de;
        }
        .highlight {
            color: #4a9d6e;
            font-weight: 600;
        }
        .highlight-warn {
            color: #dfa62e;
            font-weight: 600;
        }
        .highlight-danger {
            color: #d9463c;
            font-weight: 600;
        }

        .back-btn {
            margin-top: 30px;
            padding: 12px 30px;
            border: none;
            border-radius: 6px;
            background: #666;
            color: white;
            cursor: pointer;
            font-size: 14px;
            transition: 0.15s;
        }
        .back-btn:hover {
            background: #555;
        }
        .footer-text {
            color: #6b6558;
            font-size: 12px;
            margin-top: 30px;
            border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.04);
            padding-top: 20px;
            text-align: center;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="credits-container">
        <h1>👏 Credits</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">Ticket Rail — Smart Kitchen Order Management System</p>

        <!-- Creators -->
        <div class="credit-card">
            <h2>🎯 Created By</h2>
            <p><span class="name">Avan</span> <span class="role">— Lead Developer & System Architect</span></p>
            <p><span class="name">Tian Ning</span> <span class="role">— Developer & System Designer</span></p>
            <p style="margin-top: 10px; color: #6b6558;">
                <span class="year">© 2026</span> — Built with passion for smart kitchen automation
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- System Overview -->
        <div class="system-section">
            <h3>📋 What is Ticket Rail?</h3>
            <p>
                <strong>Ticket Rail</strong> is a <span class="highlight">real-time cooking game</span> and 
                <span class="highlight">order management system</span> that uses ESP32 microcontrollers 
                to track ingredient preparation through every step of the cooking process.
            </p>
            <p>
                The system ensures that orders are prepared correctly by <span class="highlight-warn">validating</span> 
                each ingredient's preparation status against the recipe requirements before an order can be completed.
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- How It Works -->
        <div class="system-section" style="margin-top: 16px;">
            <h3>⚙️ How It Works</h3>
            
            <p><strong>1. Hardware Components</strong></p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Tag ESP32</strong> — Passive RFID/NFC chips attached to ingredients (e.g., "Beef", "Lettuce")</li>
                <li><strong>Tagger ESP32</strong> — Station scanners placed at cooking stations (e.g., "Grill", "Prep")</li>
                <li><strong>Counter ESP32</strong> — Submission device that sends completed orders for validation</li>
            </ul>

            <p><strong>2. Setup Phase</strong></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Staff registers all ESP32 devices in the system</li>
                <li>Each Tag ESP32 is <span class="highlight">assigned to an ingredient</span> (e.g., MAC "AA:BB:CC" → "Beef")</li>
                <li>Each Tagger ESP32 is <span class="highlight">assigned to a station</span> (e.g., MAC "DD:EE:FF" → "Grill Station")</li>
                <li>Recipes are created linking ingredients to <span class="highlight-warn">required preparation steps</span></li>
            </ul>

            <p><strong>3. Order Flow</strong></p>
            <ul>
                <li><span class="highlight">Order Created</span> — System generates a new order with a unique number (e.g., "K-001")</li>
                <li><span class="highlight-warn">Ingredients Prepared</span> — Chef scans tags at stations:
                    <br>• Beef tag scanned at Grill → <span class="highlight-warn">current_status: "Default → Cook"</span>
                    <br>• Lettuce tag scanned at Prep → <span class="highlight-warn">current_status: "Default → Chop"</span>
                    <br>• Bun tag scanned at Toaster → <span class="highlight-warn">current_status: "Default → Toast"</span>
                </li>
                <li><span class="highlight">Order Submitted</span> — Counter ESP sends all scanned tag MACs to server</li>
                <li><span class="highlight-warn">Validation</span> — Server checks each tag's current_status against recipe requirements:
                    <br>• Beef → "Default → Cook" ✅ Expected: "Default → Cook"
                    <br>• Lettuce → "Default → Chop" ✅ Expected: "Default → Chop"
                    <br>• Bun → "Default → Toast" ✅ Expected: "Default → Toast"
                </li>
                <li><span class="highlight">Result</span> — If <span class="highlight">ALL PASS</span>, order is 
                    <span class="highlight">COMPLETED</span> ✅ and all tags reset to "Default"
                    <br>If <span class="highlight-danger">ANY FAIL</span>, order is <span class="highlight-danger">FAILED</span> ❌
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- System Features -->
        <div class="system-section" style="margin-top: 16px;">
            <h3>✨ Key Features</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Real-time Status Tracking</strong> — Each ingredient tag maintains a <span class="highlight-warn">status chain</span> (e.g., "Default → Chop → Cook → Plate")</li>
                <li><strong>Automatic Validation</strong> — Server automatically validates orders against recipe requirements</li>
                <li><strong>Live Game Dashboard</strong> — Visual display of active orders with ingredient status dots</li>
                <li><strong>Control Dashboard</strong> — Adjust game parameters (spawn rate, prep time, service duration)</li>
                <li><strong>ESP Monitoring</strong> — Real-time status of all connected ESP32 devices</li>
                <li><strong>Leaderboards</strong> — Track top performers by score, orders served, and accuracy</li>
                <li><strong>Recipe Management</strong> — Create and edit recipes with ingredient requirements and preparation steps</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Technology Stack -->
        <div class="system-section" style="margin-top: 16px;">
            <h3>🛠️ Technology Stack</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Backend:</strong> Node.js, Express.js, SQLite3</li>
                <li><strong>Frontend:</strong> HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript, EJS Templates</li>
                <li><strong>Hardware:</strong> ESP32 Microcontrollers, RFID/NFC Tags</li>
                <li><strong>Communication:</strong> HTTP/REST APIs, BroadcastChannel API</li>
                <li><strong>Database:</strong> SQLite with foreign key constraints and transaction support</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- System Flow Diagram -->
        <div class="system-section" style="margin-top: 16px;">
            <h3>🔄 System Flow</h3>
            <p style="font-family: 'Courier Prime', monospace; color: #6b6558; font-size: 13px; line-height: 2;">
                <span class="highlight">ESP32 Tag</span> → <span class="highlight-warn">Tagger scans</span> → <span class="highlight">Server updates status</span><br>
                <span style="color: #4a9d6e;">↓</span><br>
                <span class="highlight">Counter ESP submits</span> → <span class="highlight-warn">Server validates</span> → <span class="highlight">Order COMPLETED ✅</span><br>
                <span style="color: #d9463c;">OR</span><br>
                <span class="highlight">Counter ESP submits</span> → <span class="highlight-warn">Server validates</span> → <span class="highlight-danger">Order FAILED ❌</span>
            </p>
        </div>

        <button class="back-btn" onclick="window.location.href='/'">⬅ Back to Home</button>
        
        <div class="footer-text">
            &copy; 2026 Ticket Rail — Smart Kitchen Order Management System
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>